#! The byte-stability claim. `regions.lu` is canonical `wolf fmt` output at
#! the pin, so formatting it must produce ZERO edits — not an edit that
#! happens to be a no-op, an empty array. An editor that applies a whole-file
#! replacement on every save churns the undo stack and defeats every
#! format-on-save workflow, and the result is `exact` here for that reason.
name      requests/formatting-byte-stable
profile   minimal

initialize
open      regions.lu
wait      diagnostics regions.lu
req       formatting regions.lu
shutdown
